/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Matrix_Dynamic Dynamic Matrix
 * @ingroup Foundation_Matrix
 * @brief Runtime-sized matrix storage and operations.
 *
 * `Foundation::Math::Matrix::Dynamic<T>` allocates storage when constructed
 * with dimensions or when `Allocate()` is called. It can alternatively attach
 * to caller-owned storage; in that case the caller must keep the buffer alive
 * until the matrix is cleared, destroyed, or attached to different storage.
 *
 * @code
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Dynamic<float> matrix(3, 3);
 * matrix.At(0, 0) = 1.0f;
 * @endcode
 *
 * @warning Dynamic storage is available whenever Matrix support is enabled,
 * but embedded applications remain free to use only `Matrix::Fixed` and avoid
 * heap allocation entirely.
 *
 * @see Foundation::Math::Matrix::Dynamic
 */
